														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1581457">
									

<p>Speaking from a computer science perspective, this article has way too much information where none is needed and not enough where more is warranted. Is it the program that generates this output or the computer? Don't you think that would have been one of the first things we tested?</p>
<p>There's also way too much clutter involved; the weird titles for personnel as well as the excessive numeric designations make it hard to read. The excessive use of collapsibles in strange places also makes it hard to read from end to end and therefore hard to stay engaged. Finally, it's just simply not that interesting of an idea; at heart it's just an anomalous computer program that says spooky things then makes you go into a seizure.</p>
<p>Unfortunately I hold a much higher standard for computer-based SCPs and I have downvoted this as it does not meet said standards.</p>

